Z||000000||loafer87gt||07-03-2000||01:02 PM||||Hye guys, I installed my alarm last weekend, and while I was at it I put in a couple of rolls of "brown bread" sound deadening material. I did the whole firewall of my car, the floorboards, inside the center console and around the computer area, the difference is amazing! I can no longer hear any fuel injector clacking noise, and I can't even hear my cracked exhaust manifold ticking anymore either. I am very impressed with the stuff, on the highway there is NO exhaust drone anymore, and the car is a joy to drive now on long trips. I recommend you guys doing it to your rides as well, most stereo shops should have the material available for purchase, another big name brand is called Dynomat but it is a bit more expensive than the brown bread. Anyways, just thought I'd share this with you guys, ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Taijiguy||07-03-2000||01:11 PM||||Where did you get the stuff you're referring to? What's the approximate cost, and can it be ordered over the net?<P>Thanks,<P>Taiji<P>modified 85 GT<BR>(Soon to be 4 Barrel GT!)||||reg||1
Z||000002||overlord||07-03-2000||01:16 PM||||i will have to agree , this stuff is amazing.<P>when i had put in my subs mounted on the firewall.....various things in the enigne compartment rattled to beat all........so i bought some  "phoenix gold" sound dampener and put it on the firewall behind the sub, WOW, no rattling or vibration...and the sound inside the car sounds so much more richer.......im gettin more to do all the other areas i couldnt get at before.||||reg||1
Z||000003||loafer87gt||07-03-2000||05:44 PM||||I got mine from Direct Audio, and payed $29 a roll. It took about two rolls to do the firewall area, the floor area, and the console.||||reg||1
